        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: اصطدم",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اصطدم — iṣṭadama — \"to collide, to crash into\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اصطدمت السيارة بشجرة كبيرة. iṣṭadamat as-sayyāra bi-shajara kabīra. The car crashed into a big tree."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يصطدم, yaṣṭadim."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It takes بـ for what is hit: اصطدم (iṣṭadama) بالجدار."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اصطدم (iṣṭadama) is built on the native Arabic root ṣ-d-m (Lane), \"to strike, to knock against\". It is Form VIII, where the t turns to ṭ after ṣ: \"to strike against each other\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
